<title>UK: LME copper 'tom/next' just shy of limit in AM ring.</title>
<headline>LME copper 'tom/next' just shy of limit in AM ring.</headline>
<text>
<p>COPPER - First AM ring dominated by &quot;tom/next&quot; which traded to $24 backwardation, against $26 LME daily limit. Cash/threes $190 back, neglected three months traded at $2,265, down $13 after sizeable 17,025 tonne stock rise.</p>
<p>ALUMINIUM - Down $7 but above lows.</p>
<p>ZINC - Barely softer at $1,488. Shrugs off copper weakness.</p>
<p>NICKEL - Firmer.</p>
<p>LEAD/TIN - Weak.</p>
</text>
